Stress: dePLOY.

62
00:02:01.565 --> 00:02:02.738
Word: data.

63
00:02:03.018 --> 00:02:03.807
Stress:

64
00:02:04.087 --> 00:02:05.879
DAY-ta or DAH-ta.

65
00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:08.125
Part 3.

66
00:02:08.405 --> 00:02:09.685
Sounds to practise.

67
00:02:10.935 --> 00:02:20.962
v and w. v: top teeth touch the bottom lip, then very, video, version, server. w: round your lips, no teeth, then west, work, window, software.

68
00:02:21.242 --> 00:02:22.159
Practise:

69
00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:24.701
We will verify the new version on Wednesday.

70
00:02:26.051 --> 00:02:35.096
th. th (soft): tongue between teeth, blow air, then think, three, thanks, math. th (voiced): same, with voice, then this, that, they, other.

71
00:02:35.376 --> 00:02:36.635
Not tink or dis.

72
00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:37.832
Practise:

73
00:02:38.112 --> 00:02:40.224
Thank you, I think that's the third thing.

74
00:02:41.574 --> 00:02:42.854
s + consonant.

75
00:02:43.134 --> 00:02:50.814
Don't add a vowel before s: school not i-school, station not i-station, special not i-special, start not i-start.

76
00:02:52.164 --> 00:02:53.231
Word endings.

77
00:02:53.511 --> 00:03:01.660
Pronounce final sounds: asked (askt), world, first, texts, months. -ed endings: worked (t), played (d), waited (id).

78
00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:03.927
Part 4.

79
00:03:04.207 --> 00:03:05.829
Sentence stress and pausing.

80
00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:11.281
Stress the words that carry meaning (nouns, main verbs, numbers, not):

81
00:03:11.561 --> 00:03:14.100
The release is NOT on Friday, it's on MONDAY.

82
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.833
We reduced latency by SIXTY percent.

83
00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:19.631
Pause at commas and before important points:

84
00:03:19.911 --> 00:03:21.511
The root cause was a timeout.

85
00:03:22.861 --> 00:03:23.821
Part 5.

86
00:03:24.101 --> 00:03:25.573
Easy ways to improve.

87
00:03:26.823 --> 00:03:29.831
Shadowing: play a 30-second clip of a clear speaker.

88
00:03:30.111 --> 00:03:33.247
Repeat each sentence right after them, copying the rhythm.

89
00:03:33.527 --> 00:03:37.815
Record and compare: read a paragraph, record it, compare with the original.

90
00:03:38.095 --> 00:03:43.343
Dictionary audio: check the stress of any new word (online dictionaries have audio).

91
00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.777
Slow down by 20% in meetings.

92
00:03:46.057 --> 00:03:47.273
Clear beats fast.

93
00:03:47.553 --> 00:03:54.999
Minimal pairs: practise pairs that differ by one sound: vest or west, three or tree, ship or sheep, full or fool.

94
00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:57.287
Part 6.

95
00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.383
Conversation: when someone doesn't understand you.

96
00:04:01.633 --> 00:04:03.660
Here is how the conversation goes.

97
00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.647
Sorry, could you repeat that?

98
00:04:05.927 --> 00:04:07.185
I didn't catch it.

99
00:04:07.465 --> 00:04:08.191
Sure.

100
00:04:08.471 --> 00:04:11.820
I said we should verify the new version on Wednesday.

101
00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.020
Verify the... sorry, version?

102
00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.921
The new VERSION of the app.

103
00:04:16.201 --> 00:04:17.737
Version two point three.

104
00:04:18.017 --> 00:04:19.169
Ah, got it!

105
00:04:19.449 --> 00:04:20.879
Wednesday works for me.

106
00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:23.829
The conversation continues.

107
00:04:24.109 --> 00:04:24.855
Great.

108
00:04:25.135 --> 00:04:28.485
I'll also send it in the chat, so we have it in writing.

109
00:04:28.765 --> 00:04:29.938
Perfect, thanks.

110
00:04:31.288 --> 00:04:31.928
Tip:

111
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:34.064
Rephrase, don't repeat louder.

112
00:04:34.344 --> 00:04:39.379
If someone doesn't understand, say it more slowly, use a simpler word, or type it in chat.

113
00:04:39.659 --> 00:04:43.200
Repeating the same sentence faster or louder rarely helps.

114
00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.489
Part 7.

115
00:04:45.769 --> 00:04:46.686
Practice.

116
00:04:47.936 --> 00:04:50.176
Read these aloud and record yourself:

117
00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:59.117
We will verify the new version on Wednesday. / I think the third thing is the most important. / The developer asked the analyst for the data.

118
00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:01.342
Part 8.

119
00:05:01.622 --> 00:05:02.667
Speak today.

120
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:07.160
Shadow a 30-second clip of a clear speaker three times.

121
00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.469
Check the stress of 5 words you use every day at work.

122
00:05:10.749 --> 00:05:15.037
Slow down in one meeting and notice whether people ask you to repeat less.

123
00:05:16.387 --> 00:05:17.923
That's the end of this lesson.

124
00:05:18.203 --> 00:05:22.854
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

125
00:05:23.134 --> 00:05:29.257
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

